    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1037-a1">

                <pb facs="0986" n="728" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg728"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hubert Montgomery
                    </hi> to <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Irwin
                            Laughlin
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 24, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Laughlin</hi>: I informed Sir Edward Grey of our conversation on the 10th
                    instant, in which you told me that the State Department had renewed their
                    request to have enquiries made with regard to the telegrams referred to in the
                    notes which the Ambassador addressed to the Foreign Office in August and
                    September.</p>
                <p>
                    Sir Edward has caused the necessary
                    enquiries to be made and he wishes me to send the enclosed memorandum giving
                    their results.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hubert Montgomery</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
